David Kimmelman, vice president with GetTheJob.com, offers these networking suggestions.
The best hires come from new employees who have been referred by current employees within a company. Build a network of referrals.
For most business professionals, LinkedIn is far and away the best tool on the internet that people can use to stay connected with past, present and future colleagues. Many employers build recruiting strategies around LinkedIn because they can learn a great deal about a prospect before even interviewing them. The more business connections and friends you have on LinkedIn, the easier it will be for employers to find you.
A few key things to know:
Fill out your profile completely (you can import a resume to get you started)
Enter your past jobs and any non-profit or volunteer activities
Research the key words important to your job search and salt your profile with these terms so employers can find you
